{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "harvard-tour-pinger",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-24",
  // Two cadences, selected by day of week. Cron runs in UTC, not local time.
  //
  //   Thu-Fri  every 5 min   — both real detections landed on a Friday (Week of
  //                            08/3 at Fri 07-31 12:16Z), so this is the window
  //                            that actually needs low latency
  //   Sat-Wed  every 30 min  — nothing has ever been published on these days
  //
  // Days are spelled, not numbered, and that is deliberate. Cloudflare's
  // day-of-week field runs 1 = Sunday .. 7 = Saturday, NOT the usual 0 = Sunday
  // .. 6 = Saturday. Found the hard way: "1,31 * * * 0,1,2,3,6" was rejected
  // (`code 10100: invalid cron string`, because 0 is out of range) while "4,5"
  // was accepted in the same request — and under Cloudflare's numbering 4,5 is
  // Wed-Thu, not Thu-Fri. Valid syntax, wrong days, no error. The rejection of
  // the other leg is the only reason that did not ship. Names cannot drift.
  //
  // Deliberately encoded as one schedule rather than toggled by hand before and
  // after each Friday: a manual switch has a "forgot to change it back" failure
  // mode and this has none. Together the two legs cover all seven days with no
  // overlap — check that if you edit either one.
  //
  // Minutes are offset off :00/:30 — schedulers are busiest on round minutes,
  // and the top of the hour worst of all.
  //
  // The 5-minute leg is free only because the repo is PUBLIC, where Actions
  // minutes are unlimited. If it is ever made private the 2,000 min/month cap
  // applies and BOTH legs MUST drop back to something like "7,37 * * * *" in
  // the same sitting — otherwise the quota runs out mid-month and the workflow
  // stops firing *silently*.
  "triggers": {
    "crons": [
      "1-59/5 * * * THU,FRI",
      "1,31 * * * SAT,SUN,MON,TUE,WED"
    ]
  }
}
